)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Delimited configuration uses \code{has_header}; headerless messages also require
\code{fields}. Datetimes can come from \code{datetime_field}, with optional
\code{datetime_format} and \code{datetime_timezone}, or can be reconstructed using
\code{record_interval_seconds}, \code{record_offset_seconds}, and \code{records_order}.
Both parsers include the LRGS header fields by default; set
\code{include_lrgs_header_fields} to \code{FALSE} to omit them. Parsed text fields are
retained in \code{raw_value} and receive a missing numeric \code{value}; AquaCache does
not apply rwdm-style range clamping.
